From 56c15a07cc80634d8e4e4564be98002acd18c221 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:30:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AI_AB_TEST Economy: WarGold candidate flag, and WarChest
 saves at peace (the Aztecs' empty treasury in replay 0C3C8913)

Replay 0C3C8913: the warmonger's forced research (opening book, then
TimingBuildup's techs) has no Currency, so the Aztecs got their Market at
T103 (our other civs T55-T59). They sat at 0 gold through their window and
CP's upkeep guard refused 82 units. WarChest saved nothing: they went from
peace straight into the window at T81.

WarGold (new flag, off in the bundle), for a candidate warmonger not at war
with a major whose net gold per turn is below cities + 2, outside the window
and attack phases:
- after the opening book, research toward Currency (before TimingBuildup's techs);
- +500 for gold buildings;
- while net gold is negative (the lead's: keep income at 0 or more): no world
  wonder, no upkeep building unless it makes gold, defends, or readies the
  army (production or experience), and +300 for caravans and cargo ships.

WarChest (the lead and War): saves at peace too, from turn 30 (Standard), at
least 2 siege units' price.

Replaces patch 0021 of 5:30pm ET (same flag, on claude/ab-c1 eb4129d now).
Written 5:34pm ET.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G2NZj2nf4FeZTEHWjvnhhA
